{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-j366-h8gg-77pm","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-j366-h8gg-77pm","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-j366-h8gg-77pm","summary":"WASI preview 0 implementation of `poll_oneoff` circumvents fuel consumption","description":"## Impact\r\n\r\nThe WASI preview 0 implementation of `poll_oneoff` in `wasmtime-wasi` causes the host to do perform work which is `O(n)` in the number of subscriptions passed without consuming fuel or checking if fuel has run out. This exposes a DOS attack vector where a guest can perform long-running computations which ignore fuel limits. Systems using the `wasmtime` cli are affected because WASI preview 0 is enabled by default. Systems using `wasmtime` as a library are unaffected unless they explicitly enable WASI preview 0 via [`p0::add_to_linker_async`](https://docs.rs/wasmtime-wasi/latest/wasmtime_wasi/p0/fn.add_to_linker_async.html) or [`po::add_to_linker_sync`](https://docs.rs/wasmtime-wasi/latest/wasmtime_wasi/p0/fn.add_to_linker_sync.html)\r\n\r\nThe root cause is that the WASI preview 1 implementation of `poll_oneoff` does a fuel check, but the preview 0 version goes through an adapter which mutates each subscription before calling the WASIp1 version (and doesn't do its own fuel check).\r\n\r\nWASIp1, WASIp2, and WASIp3 are all unaffected because they either properly consume fuel or don't support this API.\r\n\r\n## Patches\r\n\r\nThe fix is present in main and patch releases are made for 36.0.17, 48.0.4 and 49.0.2.\r\n\r\n## Workarounds\r\n\r\nDisable WASI preview 0 support in the cli via `-Spreview0=n`.","severity":"medium","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"alexcrichton","id":64996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton","html_url":"https://github.com/alexcrichton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-j366-h8gg-77pm","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-02T19:45:12Z","published_at":"2026-10-02T19:39:05Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"rust","name":"wasmtime-wasi"},"vulnerable_version_range":"< 36.0.17, >= 37.0.0, < 48.0.4, >= 49.0.0, < 49.0.2","patched_versions":"36.0.17, 48.0.4, 49.0.2","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","score":4.0},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}},"cwes":[],"cwe_ids":[],"credits":[{"login":"smaeljaish771","type":"reporter"},{"login":"KeenSecurityLab","type":"sponsor"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"smaeljaish771","id":266604088,"node_id":"U_kgDOD-QOOA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266604088?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771","html_url":"https://github.com/smaeljaish771","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish771/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smaeljaish